    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0141" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg21"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Panaman Minister to the
                            Acting Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Panama</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With profound sorrow have I heard of the
                    demise of the Hon. John Hay, Secretary of State, at Newbury, N. H., at 12.25
                    this morning.</p>
                <p>The flag of the Republic of Panama will be kept at half-mast for three days as an
                    homage paid by my country to the eminent Secretary, whose death is looked upon
                    by it as a great national loss. The Republic of Panama sincerely joins in the
                    mourning of this nation for the everlasting departure of the distinguished
                    Secretary, John Hay.</p>
                <p>With sentiments of high regard, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. D. de Obaldía.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
